Terraform apply is failing due to drift, but the infra is currently live and critical. How do you fix it without causing downtime?”

1. When terraform apply fails due to drift on live we must never run a destructive command (-refresh-only with automated approvals or forcing an apply)

2. First, pull the current plan and state to see exactly what has drifted. Save the plan file so Terraform cannot execute unexpected changes.

terraform plan -out=drift_check.plan
terraform show drift_check.plan

3.If someone modified the live infrastructure manually (e.g., increased an AWS EC2 instance size or modified a security group rule during an incident) and that change needs to stay, update our Terraform configuration. 

A. Manually update our .tf files to match the exact properties currently live in production.

B. Run terraform plan again to verify that the plan now shows "No changes our infrastructure matches the configuration."

4.Re-import the live resource back into the state file 

terraform import <resource_type>.<resource_name> <actual-live-resource-id>
